   },
   "roundness": null,
   "text": "one question, drilled, carrying the findings it depends on \u2014 clear,\nvisual, obvious: no rambling, no ambiguity, no noise. a DECISION\nquestion carries five things in the simplest terms: what it is \u00b7 why\nit matters \u00b7 the gap \u00b7 what we win \u00b7 what we lose. non-simple\nquestions use the A3 storylines; a whiteboard diagram is a legitimate\nquestion form. FACTS are never asked \u2014 they die at a lower rung\n(code, docs, history). POSITIONS are never guessed \u2014 one source, the\nhuman. and STRAW-MAN YOURSELF FIRST: 'is that really true?'",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "one question, drilled, carrying the findings it depends on \u2014 clear,\nvisual, obvious: no rambling, no ambiguity, no noise. a DECISION\nquestion carries five things in the simplest terms: what it is \u00b7 why\nit matters \u00b7 the gap \u00b7 what we win \u00b7 what we lose. non-simple\nquestions use the A3 storylines; a whiteboard diagram is a legitimate\nquestion form. FACTS are never asked \u2014 they die at a lower rung\n(code, docs, history). POSITIONS are never guessed \u2014 one source, the\nhuman. and STRAW-MAN YOURSELF FIRST: 'is that really true?'",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
